WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.235
This morning, a seventy-four kilo disinfection robot drove itself

00:00:04.235 --> 00:00:07.480
to its goal. It was never built to take orders from us.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:12.000
We're Verspätete Rädfahrer, and this is how we hacked the D1.

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:16.656
The Hyundai D1 is sold as a closed box. Our track had five

00:00:16.656 --> 00:00:20.886
levels: get in, unlock every sensor, take the wheel, navigate,

00:00:20.886 --> 00:00:22.250
and answer the door.

00:00:22.867 --> 00:00:26.375
Getting in was the first wall. USB from our laptop or phone

00:00:26.375 --> 00:00:30.121
showed no device at all. So we used the robot's own touchscreen

00:00:30.121 --> 00:00:33.866
as a terminal, and gave it internet through phone tethering. We

00:00:33.866 --> 00:00:37.731
used a VPS to duplicate the robot's screen on our laptop. Then we

00:00:37.731 --> 00:00:41.477
could install Codex CLI on the D1 itself, and let the agent run

00:00:41.477 --> 00:00:42.607
loose on the robot.

00:00:43.333 --> 00:00:47.018
Inside, we found a networked brain: an Ubuntu display computer,

00:00:47.018 --> 00:00:50.644
and an internal controller running the ROS 1 master, the motor

00:00:50.644 --> 00:00:54.212
driver and the laser. We mapped the whole vendor graph before

00:00:54.212 --> 00:00:56.083
sending a single motion command.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:00.624
We ran ROS 2 Humble rootless on the display computer, with a

00:01:00.624 --> 00:01:04.639
one-way bridge from the vendor graph. Laser, odometry, IMU, the

00:01:04.639 --> 00:01:08.717
rear camera, eight air-quality sensors: thirteen topics passed a

00:01:08.717 --> 00:01:11.840
live check. Two depth cameras never sent a frame.

00:01:12.567 --> 00:01:16.254
Then, movement. Every command goes through our drive gate. It

00:01:16.254 --> 00:01:20.184
starts disarmed, clamps the speed, and drops to zero a quarter of

00:01:20.184 --> 00:01:24.113
a second after the last command. An independent watchdog cuts the

00:01:24.113 --> 00:01:25.927
motors if anything goes stale.

00:01:26.633 --> 00:01:30.519
Every drive ran as a supervised session, with a person on the red

00:01:30.519 --> 00:01:34.345
stop. Twenty-five sessions. Many of them were stopped by our own

00:01:34.345 --> 00:01:34.763
guards.

00:01:35.467 --> 00:01:39.264
The laser guard stopped us fourteen times. And three of those?

00:01:39.264 --> 00:01:43.183
The robot was seeing its own bracket. We measured it, and masked

00:01:43.183 --> 00:01:43.367
it.

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:47.421
We also killed the drive software on purpose. The watchdog

00:01:47.421 --> 00:01:49.940
tripped in a hundred and sixty milliseconds.

00:01:50.667 --> 00:01:54.216
Then came SLAM Toolbox for a live map, and Nav2 for planning.

00:01:54.216 --> 00:01:57.824
Here's the robot driving itself to a bottle that stands in for

00:01:57.824 --> 00:01:58.697
the front door.

00:02:04.567 --> 00:02:08.435
And this is a logged run from the robot's point of view. Live

00:02:08.435 --> 00:02:12.304
laser scans, the Nav2 plan, the path it drove. Ten seconds of

00:02:12.304 --> 00:02:14.397
autonomous driving. Goal reached.

00:02:16.567 --> 00:02:20.131
One point zero four metres. It stopped seventeen centimetres

00:02:20.131 --> 00:02:23.517
short, because the map shifted slightly during the drive.

00:02:24.233 --> 00:02:27.370
What we learned: the vendor's ROS 1 graph was the real

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:31.087
integration point. Published doesn't mean delivered. Motor power

00:02:31.087 --> 00:02:34.804
and motor enable are two different things. And a command timeout

00:02:34.804 --> 00:02:36.953
needs its own independent supervisor.

00:02:37.667 --> 00:02:42.077
Demonstrated: access, a ROS 2 sensor bridge, supervised driving,

00:02:42.077 --> 00:02:46.487
and a completed Nav2 goal. Next: the real door, and the doorbell

00:02:46.487 --> 00:02:50.967
through Home Assistant. It's designed, but we had no credentials.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:56.578
No flashing. No cutting. Nothing replaced. Just ROS 2. We're

00:02:56.578 --> 00:02:59.020
Verspätete Rädfahrer. Thank you!
